["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A grouse lives by its eyes and ears. Learn what it sees and hears and you get the close, calm shot instead of a roar of wings behind a tree.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 330\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of a grouse head and its field of view, using chicken data as a close cousin, 75 percent. Each eye covers a wide side wedge, for about 300 degrees in total. Only a narrow 30 degree wedge straight ahead is seen with both eyes. A small blind spot sits straight behind.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"330\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">What a grouse sees (top view)</text>\n<path d=\"M200 182 L231.1 66.1 A120 120 0 0 1 231.1 297.9 Z\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" opacity=\"1\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 182 L168.9 297.9 A120 120 0 0 1 168.9 66.1 Z\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" opacity=\"1\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 182 L231.1 297.9 A120 120 0 0 1 168.9 297.9 Z\" fill=\"#e5e5e5\" opacity=\"1\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 182 L168.9 66.1 A120 120 0 0 1 231.1 66.1 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0.8\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"188\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"168\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><polygon points=\"196,160 200,150 204,160\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n<circle cx=\"192\" cy=\"167\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#23261f\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"208\" cy=\"167\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#23261f\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Both eyes: about 30 degrees</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Left eye</text>\n<text x=\"380\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Right eye</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Blind spot behind</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Total view:</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">about 300</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"298\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">degrees</text>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Chicken data,</text>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">a close cousin</text>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"298\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">(75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Eyes on the sides: a huge field of view, little overlap <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Sees colour and motion very well <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the eyes</summary><ul><li>Grouse are galliform birds, close cousins of the chicken. Most eye studies are on chickens; treat these as a guide for grouse <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Field of view about 300 degrees, with only about 30 degrees seen by both eyes (75%, chicken data; Martin's review of bird visual fields gives 20 to 30 degrees for most birds).</li><li>A small blind spot sits straight behind the head <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Colour: four kinds of single cones (violet, blue, green, red), one more than us. Birds see colours we cannot (75%, PLOS One study on chickens).</li><li>Motion: a double cone is thought to handle motion <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. A grouse notices movement before shape (Tip, 70%).</li><li>Night: grouse roost at night in trees, on the ground or in snow <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. How well they see in the dark: no source found (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 310\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A conifer with a dark spruce grouse sitting on a branch close to the trunk, circled. It looks like a dark blob near the trunk with the tail hanging down. Tip: look up slowly; midday is the time.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"310\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Spot a grouse sitting in a tree</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"260\" width=\"400\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<rect x=\"190\" y=\"40\" width=\"16\" height=\"225\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n<path d=\"M198 70 L138 100 M198 70 L258 100\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M198 110 L108 140 M198 110 L288 140\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M198 150 L78 180 M198 150 L318 180\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M198 190 L48 220 M198 190 L348 220\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<path d=\"M198 230 L28 260 M198 230 L368 260\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(232 132) scale(0.8 0.8)\"><polygon points=\"-22,-4 -36,-8 -36,4 -22,6\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#3d3a35\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#3d3a35\"/><path d=\"M18 -20 q5 -5 10 0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c23b22\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<path d=\"M216 140 l-6 20\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\"/>\n<circle cx=\"232\" cy=\"132\" r=\"40\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<text x=\"280\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">A dark blob</text>\n<text x=\"280\" y=\"89\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">near the trunk</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Tail hangs down. Look up, slowly.</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"301\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Midday is the time (Tip).</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Move slow, stop behind trees, never skyline yourself (Tip).</li><li>Look for a shape and a twitch, not a whole bird (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how hunters use this</summary><ul><li>Your blaze orange does not hurt you much: grouse key on movement more than colour (Tip, 60%). Wear what the law and safety need.</li><li>Walk, stop, look. The stop is when you see the bird and the bird sees no motion (Tip).</li><li>In trees: scan near the trunk on the sunny side of conifers. A grouse is a dark blob with a tail hanging down (Tip).</li><li>On the ground: look for a head moving through the leaves, then freeze (Tip).</li><li>Old hand's rule (tradition): \"See the eye, not the bird.\"</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 310\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Sound chart on a frequency scale from 10 hertz to 10 kilohertz. Most birds hear best between 1 and 4 kilohertz. The grouse inner ear is tuned to low sounds below 1 kilohertz. The ruffed grouse drum is under 100 hertz. Tip: low thumps carry, like boots on rock, truck doors and voices, so talk softly and shut doors gently.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"310\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">What grouse hear</text>\n<line x1=\"30\" y1=\"226\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"226\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<line x1=\"30.0\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"30.0\" y2=\"232\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"30.0\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10 Hz</text>\n<line x1=\"143.33333333333331\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"143.33333333333331\" y2=\"232\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"143.33333333333331\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100 Hz</text>\n<line x1=\"256.66666666666663\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"256.66666666666663\" y2=\"232\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"256.66666666666663\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1 kHz</text>\n<line x1=\"370.0\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"370.0\" y2=\"232\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"370.0\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10 kHz</text>\n<text x=\"84.07374220156174\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ruffed drum: under 100 Hz</text>\n<rect x=\"84.07374220156174\" y=\"78\" width=\"54.07374220156174\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fbe3d3\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"143.33333333333331\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Grouse inner ear: tuned below 1 kHz</text>\n<rect x=\"143.33333333333331\" y=\"132\" width=\"113.33333333333331\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8ecd9\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"324.9001323505024\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Most birds hear best: 1 to 4 kHz</text>\n<rect x=\"256.66666666666663\" y=\"184\" width=\"68.23346568383579\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Low thumps carry: boots on rock, truck doors,</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"298\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">voices. Talk soft, shut doors gently (Tip).</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Most birds hear best at 1 to 4 kHz <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Grouse ears are tuned to low sounds <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what grouse hear</summary><ul><li>Bird hearing is sharpest between 1 and 4 kHz, about where we hear best (70%, bird hearing reviews).</li><li>Gallinaceous birds (grouse, quail, chickens) have an inner ear tuned lower, below 1 kHz <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Chickens hear very low sounds, under 64 Hz, better than people <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>The ruffed grouse drum is a very low sound, under 100 Hz <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>. Other grouse hear it a long way off.</li><li>What carries to a grouse: boots on rock, a slammed truck door, a dropped tailgate, voices (Tip).</li><li>Tip: close doors gently, talk in a whisper, and do not crunch along a gravel road edge.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, top view. Wind blows from the grouse toward you. The grouse scent drifts downwind in a widening cone. Your dog zig zags into the wind, crosses the scent cone, turns up it and closes on the grouse. Point or flush: be ready.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Your dog works into the wind</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"260\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n<g><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"270.0\" y2=\"70.0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"270.0,70.0 279.0,65.7 279.0,74.3\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;-20 0;0 0\" dur=\"2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g>\n<g><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"270.0\" y2=\"120.0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"270.0,120.0 279.0,115.7 279.0,124.3\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;-20 0;0 0\" dur=\"2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Wind</text>\n<path d=\"M300 170 L80 110 L80 230 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".18\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(300 170)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"8\" rx=\"30\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(302 168) scale(0.55 0.55)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<text x=\"300\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Grouse</text>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Scent drifts downwind</text>\n<path id=\"mgr-dog-wind-p\" d=\"M40 280 L120 250 L40 210 L130 175 L170 168 L240 170\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 6\"/>\n<g><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><animateMotion dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\"><mpath href=\"#mgr-dog-wind-p\"/></animateMotion></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hits the scent!</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"48\" width=\"230\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"125\" y=\"69\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Point or flush: be ready</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Your dog finds the scent cone downwind. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>No study found that grouse smell people (Tip).</li><li>Wind matters for sound and for your dog's nose (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: wind and thermals for a grouse hunter</summary><ul><li>Birds of the grouse family are not known for a strong sense of smell. We found no source showing grouse detect hunters by scent (Tip, so treat smell as a minor factor).</li><li>Wind carries your noise toward or away from the bird (Tip).</li><li>Wind and rising or sinking air (thermals) carry the bird's scent to your dog. Work a dog into the wind so it meets the scent cone (Tip, common dog handling advice).</li><li>Thermals: air rises up slopes when the sun warms them and sinks at evening (80%, see <a href=\"#/s/wind-thermals\">Wind and thermals</a>).</li><li>Strong wind seems to make grouse wild. Hunters blame noise that hides predators (hunter lore, 60%). See <a href=\"#/s/mc-grouse-06\">The day</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 330\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The grouse escape plan in 5 steps. 1: freeze and trust the camouflage. 2: walk or run off under cover. 3: flush with a roar of wings. 4: glide, usually under 90 metres or 100 yards. 5: land in a tree or cover and freeze again.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"330\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Grouse escape plan: 5 steps</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"46\" width=\"372\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<circle cx=\"36\" cy=\"69\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"36\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text>\n<text x=\"58\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Freeze. Trust the camouflage.</text>\n<rect x=\"28\" y=\"102\" width=\"358\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"125\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"50\" y=\"131\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text>\n<text x=\"72\" y=\"131\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Walk or run off under cover.</text>\n<rect x=\"42\" y=\"158\" width=\"344\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fbe3d3\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"181\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"64\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text>\n<text x=\"86\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Flush with a roar of wings.</text>\n<rect x=\"56\" y=\"214\" width=\"330\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<circle cx=\"78\" cy=\"237\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"78\" y=\"243\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text>\n<text x=\"100\" y=\"243\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Glide, usually under 90 m (100 yd).</text>\n<rect x=\"70\" y=\"270\" width=\"316\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<circle cx=\"92\" cy=\"293\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"92\" y=\"299\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">5</text>\n<text x=\"114\" y=\"299\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Land in a tree or cover. Freeze again.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>First defence: camouflage and stillness <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Last: a roaring flush and a short glide to cover <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the escape plan, in detail</summary><ul><li>Spruce grouse rely on camouflage and stillness and often let people close <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Ruffed grouse often walk or run away under cover before they fly (Tip, 65%).</li><li>The flush is loud on purpose: the roar startles a predator (Tip, 60%).</li><li>After the flush a ruffed grouse glides, usually under 90 m (100 yd), and often lands in a tree (75%, Pennsylvania Game Commission; Outdoor Life).</li><li>Then it freezes again. That is why a follow up works (Tip). See <a href=\"#/s/mc-grouse-04\">The mind</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, side view of a forest edge. You walk slowly along the edge. You stop and stand still. The grouse hiding ahead cannot stand the silence and flushes with a roar of wings, climbing up and away over the trees. Up and away with sky behind it is the safe shot. Tip: the stop makes the bird flush.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"200\" width=\"400\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"170\" width=\"400\" height=\"34\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" opacity=\".5\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\" transform=\"translate(40 200) scale(1.4)\"><polygon points=\"-12,0 0,-34 12,0\"/><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"0\" width=\"6\" height=\"8\"/></g>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\" transform=\"translate(360 200) scale(1.6)\"><polygon points=\"-12,0 0,-34 12,0\"/><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"0\" width=\"6\" height=\"8\"/></g>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\" transform=\"translate(300 196) scale(1.1)\"><polygon points=\"-12,0 0,-34 12,0\"/><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"0\" width=\"6\" height=\"8\"/></g>\n  <g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(1.0)\"><circle r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><rect x=\"-6\" y=\"8\" width=\"12\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"40 216;160 216;160 216\" keyTimes=\"0;.45;1\" dur=\"8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n  <g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.8)\"><path d=\"M-18 -4 L-30 -14.0 L-30 2 Z\" fill=\"#8a7560\"/><ellipse rx=\"22\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#8a7560\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#8a7560\"/><path d=\"M14 -24 Q20 -36 26 -30\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M26 -15 L32 -13 L26 -11Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-4 14 L-6 24 M6 14 L8 24\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"250 196;250 196;290 130;340 96\" keyTimes=\"0;.62;.8;1\" dur=\"8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"6.4s\"/><path d=\"M230 170 l-14 -10 M240 160 l-6 -16 M262 160 l6 -16 M272 170 l14 -10\"/></g>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"380\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <g><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"3.6s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Walk slowly along the edge</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"3.6s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"5s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stop. Stand still...</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The stop makes it flush (Tip)</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"7.2s\"/><rect x=\"190\" y=\"240\" width=\"204\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"292\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Up and away, sky behind:</text><text x=\"292\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">now it is a safe shot</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Walk, stop, wait. The stop flushes the bird. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Walk slow, stop often: the silence makes the bird nervous (Tip).</li><li>Be ready when you stop, not when you walk (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why the stop works (hunter lore)</summary><ul><li>Many hunting writers say a grouse holds while you keep walking past, then flushes when you stop, because a stopped predator may have seen it (hunter lore, 60%).</li><li>Stop next to an opening with room to swing, not in the thick of it (Tip).</li><li>Hold the gun at ready during the stop (Tip).</li><li>Circle a lone evergreen: a grouse under it may walk to the far side and flush from there (Tip, Outdoor Canada).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 330\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of a grouse head and its field of view, using chicken data as a close cousin, 75 percent. Each eye covers a wide side wedge, for about 300 degrees in total. Only a narrow 30 degree wedge straight ahead is seen with both eyes. A small blind spot sits straight behind.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"330\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">What a grouse sees (top view)</text>\n<path d=\"M200 182 L231.1 66.1 A120 120 0 0 1 231.1 297.9 Z\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" opacity=\"1\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 182 L168.9 297.9 A120 120 0 0 1 168.9 66.1 Z\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" opacity=\"1\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 182 L231.1 297.9 A120 120 0 0 1 168.9 297.9 Z\" fill=\"#e5e5e5\" opacity=\"1\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 182 L168.9 66.1 A120 120 0 0 1 231.1 66.1 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0.8\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"188\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"168\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><polygon points=\"196,160 200,150 204,160\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n<circle cx=\"192\" cy=\"167\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#23261f\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"208\" cy=\"167\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#23261f\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Both eyes: about 30 degrees</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Left eye</text>\n<text x=\"380\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Right eye</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Blind spot behind</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Total view:</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">about 300</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"298\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">degrees</text>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Chicken data,</text>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">a close cousin</text>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"298\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">(75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Rhyme: \"It sees you move, it hears you step, it never smells the sweat you've kept.\"</li><li>Number trick: \"300 to see, 30 to judge\": 300 degree view, 30 degrees with both eyes.</li><li>Old hand's rule (tradition): \"Walk like you're late, stop like you're lost.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li>\"Stop where you can swing.\"</li><li>\"Doors soft, voices low.\"</li><li>\"Dog into the wind, you behind the dog.\"</li><li>These are memory lines made for this course and widely repeated hunter habits, not science.</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>Chicken vision and bird hearing studies, Pennsylvania Game Commission, hunting writers. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source</summary><ul><li>Kram, Mantey and Corbo, avian cone photoreceptors (PLOS One), search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://research.birmingham.ac.uk/en/publications/visual-fields-and-their-functions-in-birds\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Martin, Visual fields and their functions in birds</a>, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Bird hearing: reviews of avian audiograms, chicken and quail studies, ruffed grouse inner ear abstract, search previews (65 to 70%).</li><li><a href=\"https://www.pa.gov/agencies/pgc/wildlife/discover-pa-wildlife/ruffed-grouse\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Pennsylvania Game Commission, Ruffed grouse</a>, read directly <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.outdoorlife.com/articles/hunting/2007/09/hit-or-miss-grouse\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outdoor Life, Hit or miss grouse</a>, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.outdoorcanada.ca/?p=68\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outdoor Canada, Ruffed grouse tips</a>, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://idfg.idaho.gov/press/field-forest-grouse\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Idaho Fish and Game, Field and forest grouse</a>, read directly <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>All checked 2026-10-11. Full log: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-grouse.md</code>.</li></ul></details>"]